# Godot 4
.godot/
/android/
*.translation

# export_presets.cfg is deliberately NOT ignored, though Godot's own template
# ignores it. It carries no credentials here — code signing is off and the
# remote-deploy block is stock — and it is the only record of what a shippable
# build actually excludes (tools/, assets/, docs/). Ignoring it would mean
# "there is an export preset" was a claim nobody else could check out.
# If signing is ever enabled, move the certificate path into a local override
# rather than committing it.

# Build output
build/
*.exe
*.pck
*.zip
!assets/**/*.zip

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Scratch
scratch/
*.log

# Redundant source-art formats (the glTF copies are what the game imports).
# Kept on disk, kept out of the repo to hold clone size down.
assets/Stylized_Nature_MegaKitStandard/FBX/
assets/Stylized_Nature_MegaKitStandard/FBX (Unity)/
assets/Stylized_Nature_MegaKitStandard/OBJ/
assets/Stylized_Nature_MegaKitStandard/Textures/
assets/source/Mushroom/base.obj
desktop.ini

# The old pipeline's rejected Mixamo downloads, if a clone still has them on
# disk. Nothing reads them since D-101; delete the folder when you like.
assets/source/_rejected/

# The raw Rust arena export: 337 MB, which is over GitHub's 100 MB single-file
# limit, so it cannot be committed even if we wanted to carry it. 333 MB of that
# is fifty-two lossless 2K PNGs. `python tools/prepare_map.py` turns it into the
# committed art/maps/rust/rust.glb (~43 MB) and is the only thing that needs it,
# so the raw file lives in the team's shared drive and gets dropped back at this
# path — Downloads included — whenever the map is re-exported.
assets/source/Rust/rust.glb

# The Tripo retexture downloads the thirteen team skins are extracted from
# (D-108): one .glb per skin, each a whole copy of the body, and the committed
# thing is `art/skins/<name>/basecolor.png` that `tools/extract_skins.py` pulls
# out of it. `assets/source/skins/README.md` says so.
assets/source/skins/*/*.glb

# ...and the other half of the same problem, at the other end of the pipeline.
# `gltf/embedded_image_handling` is set to Extract, which is the right setting —
# it gets each of the map's 51 textures its own `.import` and its own VRAM
# compression — but it means Godot writes all 41 MB of them back out beside the
# `.glb` they came from, byte for byte. Committing those would very nearly
# double the map's cost in the repository to store nothing that is not already
# in the file next to them.
#
# They are regenerated by the import step, which is the first thing
# `tools/smoke_test.sh` does and the first thing the editor does on a fresh
# clone, so there is nothing to do by hand. The `.glb` and its `.import` are
# kept: the first is the map and the second is how it is imported, and neither
# can be derived from anything else.
art/maps/*/*
!art/maps/*/*.glb
!art/maps/*/*.glb.import

# Smoke-test logs and frames
.smoke/

# Preview and range-tool renders
out/

# The BOG's base-colour texture is extracted from art/bog/BOG.fbx by the import
# step, 12 MB of PNG regenerated every time the body is re-imported, so it is
# kept out of the repository the same way the map textures are above. The
# embedded image is a JPEG named BOG_basecolor.jpg inside the FBX; Godot writes
# it out under the image's index as a PNG, which is why the name is BOG_0.png.
#
# The `.import` beside it is ignored *with* it, and that pairing is the whole
# point (D-095's second trap): a texture's `.import` carries a
# `generator_parameters/md5`, and on a checkout that has the `.import` without
# the file the importer matches the md5, decides the extraction is up to date
# and never runs it. The body then imports with `Image index '0' couldn't be
# loaded`, its material gets no albedo texture, and the team-tint shader samples
# default white — a flat grey BOG, with nothing in the log once the first import
# has scrolled past. They are derived together and they are ignored together;
# committing either one alone is the bug. `tools/clip_check.gd` fails loudly on
# the symptom; the cure is to delete both, run the import twice (the extraction
# cannot feed the pass that runs it, so the first pass writes the PNG and the
# second imports it), then delete the body's cached scene
# `.godot/imported/BOG.fbx-*` and import once more, which is the pass that
# builds the material on a texture that loads.
art/bog/BOG_0.png
art/bog/BOG_0.png.import

# Voice memos dropped in for triage: big audio, not game content. Kept out of
# the repo (GitHub caps single files at 100 MB) and out of the export by the
# .gdignore beside them.
memos/*
!memos/.gdignore

# The raw quarry pack: 5 GB of Tripo exports, trimmed into art/maps/quarry/ by
# tools/trim_quarry_pack.py. Never committed, and hidden from Godot by .gdignore.
assets/quarry_asset_pack/
